"" print

"A sorting network for n wires is a fixed sequence of compare-and-swaps" print
"that sorts ANY input permutation." print
"" print

"Key insight: Networks are DATA-OBLIVIOUS - same operations regardless of input" print
"This makes them ideal for:" print
"  - Parallel/SIMD implementations" print
"  - Cryptographic applications (constant-time)" print
"  - Hardware sorting circuits" print
"" print

"━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━" print
